WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.780
Coding Exercise 3 uses the anti-join pattern You
need patients

00:00:05.806 --> 00:00:11.565
who do not have any lab results Start by preserving
all patients

00:00:12.476 --> 00:00:16.647
Then try to match lab rows For patients with no
match the

00:00:16.673 --> 00:00:22.075
right-side lab columns will be NULL Choose a
right-side column that cannot

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:26.328
be NULL on a real matched lab row The primary key
test

00:00:26.354 --> 00:00:31.768
ID is a good choice Then filter for that key being
missing

00:00:33.506 --> 00:00:37.956
Run and Check and inspect how many patients are
returned In this

00:00:37.982 --> 00:00:43.538
practice database the expected set is small Read
your query as

00:00:43.564 --> 00:00:47.485
a sentence keep patients try to match lab results
then keep only

00:00:47.511 --> 00:00:52.519
the patients for whom no lab result was found This
pattern is

00:00:52.545 --> 00:00:57.111
widely useful for data-quality and operational
questions about missing relationships
